</div>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Based on the graph, what is the approximate height, in feet, of Player A’s baseball when hit? How do you know?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>We can look at the \(y\)-intercept of the graph, and it looks like the \(y\)-coordinate is about 5.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="d3edcdac-e79a-484c-a6fd-f94d8072c5d5" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="41ccb94e-1b66-4125-afd1-e40694755a1a" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="4">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the height, in feet, of Player B’s baseball when hit?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here: <emphasis/></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 4 feet. Find the height when \(t=0\). \(g(0)=(-16(0)−1)(0−4)=(-1)(-4)=4\), so it was hit at 4 feet.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
